From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 05:06:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BD-J host: ready for systemd after the greeting, and gone
 with its player

The image runs one host per disc (hades-bdj@.service, Accept=yes). A host
stuck before it greeted the player stayed until RuntimeMaxSec (24 h), with up
to 1 GiB and a processor: the player gives up after 30 s, but without the
greeting it does not know the host's pid. A host whose player went away (Kodi
ended, crashed or restarted) stayed for as long as the disc's Java kept the
closing from finishing, and with Accept=yes systemd cannot see that.

- hades-bdj-host speaks systemd's readiness protocol (sd_notify, without
  libsystemd). It opens $NOTIFY_SOCKET first thing, before its filter, and
  removes the variable from the environment. READY=1 goes out once the player
  is greeted, before anything of the disc is read (BD_BDJ_HOST_CONFIG.ready),
  and the socket is closed. The units wait for it (Type=notify) and kill the
  whole instance when it does not come in time.
- Its filter refuses datagram sockets of AF_UNIX: nothing that runs after it
  (the JVM, the disc's code) can write to systemd's notification socket. A
  stream socket cannot connect to it.
- bd_bdj_host_run(): a thread of its own waits for the end of the connection
  (POLLRDHUP). The disc is then closed in order, and if that does not finish
  in 5 s the process ends (_exit()). As PID 1 of its own PID namespace
  (PrivatePIDs=), everything the disc started ends with it.

Measured with the systemd of the build host (259) and the units of the tree:
the host is ready 57 ms after its start (119 ms on two processors shared with
32 busy loops); one that never answers the greeting is killed at 30 s, with
nothing of it left; with a disc whose Java never ends (a key handler that never
returns: the shutdown of libbluray waits for its thread without a limit) and
the player killed, the host ends 5.0 s later.
